messages.content:
Relaxing lines 108–110 lets execution continue past the status gate into the remaining guards in `signFieldWithToken`. Neither opened caller adds its own `DocumentStatus` check before delegating, so both call sites can reach the modified code with envelopes in statuses other than `PENDING`. Passing the changed guard does not guarantee reaching the transaction writes — several guards remain.

**Verified call paths and conditions**

```
108:110:packages/lib/server-only/field/sign-field-with-token.ts
  if (envelope.status !== DocumentStatus.PENDING) {
    throw new Error(`Document ${envelope.id} must be pending for signing`);
  }
```

`field-router/router.ts` (lines 615–633) defines `signFieldWithToken` on `procedure` (not `authenticatedProcedure`) with `ctx.user?.id` optional. No document-status check appears in the handler before the call. The `procedure` middleware and `ZSignFieldWithTokenMutationSchema` were not opened; their constraints are unverified.

```
615:633:packages/trpc/server/field-router/router.ts
  signFieldWithToken: procedure.input(ZSignFieldWithTokenMutationSchema).mutation(async ({ input, ctx }) => {
    const { token, fieldId, value, isBase64, authOptions } = input;

    ctx.logger.info({
      input: {
        fieldId,
      },
    });

    return await signFieldWithToken({
      token,
      fieldId,
      value: value ?? '',
      isBase64,
      userId: ctx.user?.id,
      authOptions,
      requestMetadata: ctx.metadata.requestMetadata,
    });
  }),
```

`apply-multi-sign-signature.ts` also uses `procedure` (line 15). Three caller-side guards precede each `signFieldWithToken` call: unviewed-document rejection (line 35), additional-auth rejection (lines 48–55), and a skip for `SigningStatus.REJECTED` recipients (line 61). The field query at lines 65–72 additionally filters to `FieldType.SIGNATURE` with `inserted: false`. No `DocumentStatus` check appears in this handler. `getDocumentByToken` and `getRecipientByToken` (lines 25–26) were not opened — whether either filters by status is unknown.

```
61:84:packages/trpc/server/embedding-router/apply-multi-sign-signature.ts
          if (envelope.recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.REJECTED) {
            return;
          }

          const signatureFields = await prisma.field.findMany({
            where: {
              envelopeId: envelope.document.id,
              recipientId: envelope.recipient.id,
              type: FieldType.SIGNATURE,
              inserted: false,
            },
          });

          await Promise.all(
            signatureFields.map(async (field) =>
              signFieldWithToken({
                token: envelope.recipient.token,
                fieldId: field.id,
                value: signature,
                isBase64,
                requestMetadata: metadata.requestMetadata,
              }),
            ),
          );
```

After the changed guard, the target enforces: `assertRecipientNotExpired(recipient)` (line 112, implementation unread); `signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED` for the token recipient or `field.recipient` (line 114); `field.inserted` (line 118); per-type field validations (lines 127–172); `validateFieldAuth(...)` (line 174, implementation unread); signature presence and typed-signature restrictions (lines 203–209); and readOnly default-value enforcement (lines 211–231).

Within `prisma.$transaction`, `tx.field.update` (lines 237–245) runs unconditionally, setting `customText` and `inserted: true`. `tx.signature.upsert` runs only when `isSignatureField` is true:

```
247:262:packages/lib/server-only/field/sign-field-with-token.ts
    if (isSignatureField) {
      const signature = await tx.signature.upsert({
        where: {
          fieldId: field.id,
        },
        create: {
          fieldId: field.id,
          recipientId: field.recipientId,
          signatureImageAsBase64: signatureImageAsBase64,
          typedSignature: typedSignature,
        },
        update: {
          signatureImageAsBase64: signatureImageAsBase64,
          typedSignature: typedSignature,
        },
      });
```

Its `create` path fires when no signature row exists for `fieldId`; `update` overwrites both `signatureImageAsBase64` and `typedSignature`. `tx.documentAuditLog.create` (lines 270–309) runs unconditionally inside the transaction.

**Pre-ship verification**

1. **`getDocumentByToken` and `getRecipientByToken`:** Open both bodies — either may carry an indirect status filter not visible in `apply-multi-sign-signature.ts`'s own body.
2. **`assertRecipientNotExpired` and `validateFieldAuth`:** Both execute before the transaction; their rejection conditions are not established by name alone — open their bodies.
3. **`procedure` middleware (both callers):** Both callers use `procedure`, not `authenticatedProcedure`; the middleware was not opened, so authentication and authorization requirements cannot be inferred from the procedure name or the optional `userId` field.
4. **Remaining inline guards for non-PENDING envelopes:** Establish whether `signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED` (line 114) and `field.inserted` (line 118) reliably prevent writes for documents in other statuses — the opened bodies do not establish what those fields contain for non-PENDING records.
